A||N||5||GT-maniac||transmission woes||||8||
Z||000000||GT-maniac||06-29-2000||02:48 PM||||My car has now decided it doesn't want to shift into second anymore. My question is what will be cheaper replacing the tranny with a another one (assuming I can find one) or having it repaired. It has been grinding when I shift into second for awhile now so I've been shifting more slowly. Any other ways I can fix this short of shelling out big bucks ?||||reg||8
Z||000001||GT-maniac||06-29-2000||02:49 PM||||Forgot to add it's the 4 spd muncie in my car||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||06-29-2000||02:54 PM||||<BR>What makes you think it is the transmission?<P>The clutch pedal, master cylinder, slave cylinder, or lack of oil may be causing the problem.<P>When was the last time you bled the system?<P>If you do this and you still have a problem, the clutch itself may be going, then just replace the parts that are bad, don't replace the tranny.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||06-29-2000||04:30 PM||||My two cents says it wouldn't hurt to check shift linkage, too.  Check adjusting nuts (@ levers on the transmission end of cables) for looseness.  Also, big nut that attaches levers to shift shaft.<P>Try adjusting cables. Maybe it grinds because it's not fully getting into gear.<P>If this works, shell out small bucks to me at.....     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">    <P><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 06-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||dman||06-29-2000||06:03 PM||||Hi GT-Maniac. I don't know if it is a transmission problem or not but you may wish to examine the slave cylinder bracket. The 4 speed muncies used a cast aluminum bracket that has a tendency to break (or at least flex). Sometimes the pushrod coming out of the slave is at an angle instead of being directly in line, this contributes to the flex and breakage problem.<P>An old GT parts car that I had suffered from this problem. It also needed an adjustment to the selector cable. It had problems shifting into 1st and 2nd I think. Upon inspection it turned out the bracket had broken and the previous owner used a couple of washers to help bolt down the cracked piece. This resulted in even more flex. Rodney Dickman makes a steel replacement that won't flex or break, I believe OEM parts from GM are no longer in production. <P>Have someone depress the clutch pedal while you examine the slave cylinder. Make sure there is no flex and that the range of travel seems appropriate.<P>You may also wish to double check your cable adjustments. If they are off, it could lead to the problem you are describing.<P>Good luck and I hope you get your fiero fixed up.||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT-maniac||06-29-2000||09:04 PM||||Thanks for the replies everyone. I changed my tranny fluid and it is shifting better for now. I'll keep my fingers crossed...<BR>||||reg||1
